.gitignore
# Dokploy writes the configured env vars to `.env` in the build context just
# before `docker build` (createEnvFile: true). Letting that one through is
# how NEXT_PUBLIC_* get baked into the JS bundle at `next build` time. Local
# `.env.local` etc. would only matter if the build ran on a developer
# machine — Dokploy clones fresh, so they never exist on the build server.
.env.local
.env.*.local
.DS_Store
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.vercel
